  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has an array AAA of size NNN such that 1≤Ai≤K1 \\le A_i \\le K1≤Ai​≤K for all 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N. \\\\\nChef also has another array BBB of size MMM such that 1≤Bi≤K1 \\le B_i \\le K1≤Bi​≤K for all 1≤i≤M1 \\le i \\le M1≤i≤M\n\nChef can perform the following operation: \\\\\n**1)** Select an integer XXX such that 1≤X≤K1 \\le X \\le K1≤X≤K \\\\\n**2)** Append XXX to the end of exactly one array among AAA and BBB\n\nFind the **minimum** number of operations required to make mean(A)mean(A)mean(A) **strictly** greater than mean(B)mean(B)mean(B) or determine it is not possible to do so.\n\nFor an array XXX of length MMM, mean(X)mean(X)mean(X) is defined as ΣXiM\\frac{\\Sigma X_i}{M}MΣXi​​. For example,\n\n\nmean([5,6])=5+62=5.5mean([5, 6]) = \\frac{5+6}{2} = 5.5mean([5,6])=25+6​=5.5\nmean([10,13,20])=10+13+203=14.333...mean([10, 13, 20]) = \\frac{10+13+20}{3} = 14.333...mean([10,13,20])=310+13+20​=14.333...\nmean([3,3,3,3,3])=3mean([3, 3, 3, 3, 3]) = 3mean([3,3,3,3,3])=3\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains three space-separated integers NNN, MMM and KKK - the size of array AAA, the size of array BBB and the upper bound of values in arrays AAA and BBB.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers A1A_1A1​, A2A_2A2​, ..., ANA_NAN​ denoting the array AAA.\nThe third line contains MMM space-separated integers B1B_1B1​, B2B_2B2​, ..., BMB_MBM​ denoting the array BBB.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the minimum number of operations required to make mean(A)&gt;mean(B)mean(A) &gt; mean(B)mean(A)&gt;mean(B).\n\n\nOutput −1-1−1 if it is not possible to do so.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N,M≤1051 \\leq N, M \\leq 10^51≤N,M≤105",
      "1≤K≤1061 \\leq K \\leq 10^61≤K≤106",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤K1 \\leq A_i, B_i \\leq K1≤Ai​,Bi​≤K",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10510^5105.",
      "Sum of MMM over all test cases won't exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
